    fix: "Wrap the parse in try/catch and respond 400 on failure, e.g. `let data; try { data = JSON.parse(req.body); } catch { return res.status(400).end(); }`, or validate with a schema (zod/Joi) first. If a body parser already ran, use req.body directly instead of re-parsing. Note `|| '{}'` / `?? '{}'` is not a fix — it does not catch malformed JSON.",
